#######
# Setup
#######

$name = randomPerson();
$initial = 425;
$rate = random(20,30);
$final = random(200,300,25);
Context("LinearRelation")->variables->are(t => 'Real');
$equation = LinearRelation("$initial - $rate t = $final");

#############################
# Exercise Group Introduction
#############################

BEGIN_PGML
Write an equation to model the scenario. There is no need to solve the equation.

END_PGML

######
# Body
######

BEGIN_PGML
[$name] baked a pie at [`[$initial]\,^{\circ}F`] and just took it out of the oven. It immediately starts to cool at a rate of [`[$rate]\,\frac{^{\circ}F}{\text{min}}\text{.}`] How long will it take to cool to [`[$final]\,^{\circ}F\text{?}`] Write an equation to model this scenario. There is no need to solve it.

[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|t|]* as the variable.')@]**

[_]{$equation}{20}

END_PGML

